# Flattened DUTs are NOT tracked in this area, deliberately.
#
# Elsewhere in formal/ the sv2v output is committed, and a staleness audit found
# 36 of 48 flat files no longer matching their RTL. A stale flat file is the
# worst kind of failure: the proof still runs, still passes, and is proving
# something about RTL that no longer exists. Untracked, the file cannot exist
# until make builds it from the current sources, so the failure mode is gone
# rather than merely watched for.
*_flat.v

# sby output. Listed by ARTIFACT rather than by workdir name: the per-task dir
# is <block>_<task>/, but a bare `sby -f x.sby` writes to <block>/ instead, and
# a per-block list of both shapes would need a new line for every block added.
# Ignoring what sby puts INSIDE a workdir covers every shape, now and later.
# the workdir itself, for the task names used here
*_prove/
*_cover/
*_data/
# ...and its contents by name, so a task named something else still cannot leak
status.sqlite
config.sby
logfile.txt
model/
src/
engine_*/
*.xml
PASS
FAIL
ERROR
TIMEOUT
UNKNOWN
status
status.path
